mall\">V\u003C/hi>\u003C/hi>\u003C/num>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"4\"/>uxori dulcissi\u003Chi rend=\"ligature\">mae\u003C/hi>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"5\"/>Iulius Demetri\n                    \u003Clb n=\"6\" break=\"no\"/>us maritus q\u003Chi rend=\"ligature\">ua\u003C/hi>\u003Chi rend=\"small\">e\u003C/hi>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"7\"/>vixit cum suo\n                    \u003Clb n=\"8\"/>marito \u003Cexpan>\u003Cabbr>ann\u003C/abbr>\u003Cex>os\u003C/ex>\u003C/expan> \u003Cnum value=\"15\">\u003Chi rend=\"supraline\">X\u003Chi rend=\"small\">V\u003C/hi>\u003C/hi>\u003C/num>\n                    \u003Clb n=\"9\"/>libenti animo\n                \u003C/ab>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"apparatus\">\n                \u003ClistApp>\u003Capp>\u003Cnote>text after Bivona corrected against photographs\u003C/note>\u003C/app>\u003C/listApp>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"translation\" xml:lang=\"en\" resp=\"#JP\">\n                \u003Cp>Crispia Salvia lived for more or less 45 years. Iulius Demetrius her husband (set this up) for his most beloved wife, who lived with her husband for 15 years with a cheerful spirit.\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"commentary\">\n                \u003Cp>\u003C!--commented out pending revision-->\n                    \u003C!--In a unique tomb, of 6 burials, hypogeum type, walls painted. In memory of Crispia Salvia. Now seen on display in Baglio Anselmi, where the right side appears to be missing-->\u003C/p>\n            \u003C/div>\n            \u003Cdiv type=\"bibliography\">\n                \u003ClistBibl type=\"edition\">\n                    \u003Cbibl type=\"bulletin\" n=\"AE\">\n                        \u003Cdate>2000\u003C/date>\n                        \u003CcitedRange>641\u003C/citedRange>\n                        \u003Cptr target=\"https://www.zotero.org/groups/382445/items/R46KDTZX\"/>\n                    \u003Cref target=\"